      "target": "../sections/sec-front-matter.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Homa at SemEval-2025 Task 5: Aligning Librarian Records with\nOntoAligner for Subject Tagging\nHadi Bayrami Asl Tekanlou1, Jafar Razmara1, Mahsa Sanaei1,\nMostafa Rahgouy2, Hamed Babaei Giglou3\n1University of Tabriz, Tabriz, Iran\nh.bayrami1403@ms.tabrizu.ac.ir,razmara@tabrizu.ac.ir,mahsa.san75@gmail.com\n2Auburn University, Alabama, USA\nmzr0108@auburn.edu\n3TIB - Leibniz Information Centre for Science and Technology, Hannover, Germany\nhamed.babaei@tib.eu\nAbstract\nThis paper presents our system, Homa, for\nSemEval-2025 Task 5: Subject Tagging, which\nfocuses on automatically assigning subject la-\nbels",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Title, authors and abstract of \"Homa at SemEval-2025 Task 5: Aligning Librarian Records with OntoAligner for Subject Tagging\" by Bayrami Asl Tekanlou, Razmara, Sanaei, Rahgouy and Babaei Giglou (University of Tabriz, Auburn University, TIB Hannover). The Homa system assigns subject labels from the Gemeinsame Normdatei (GND) taxonomy to technical records from TIBKAT. It uses OntoAligner, a modular ontology-alignment toolkit, with retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), treating subject tagging as an alignment task in which records are matched to GND categories by semantic similarity. The authors evaluate how well OntoAligner adapts to subject indexing and multilingual records, and report both strengths and limitations.",
