      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Rest of fine-tuning, the dataset and the quantitative results, with the text layers of Table 2 and Figures 1–3. The LLM was fine-tuned on 12,348 samples (at most 200 pairs per record) with QLoRA, as a match/no-match classifier, for 10 epochs at batch size 8 with 8-bit Paged AdamW. The TIB-Core-Subjects dataset has 15,263 records in five types (article, book, conference, report, thesis) in English and German, split 7,632 / 3,728 / 3,948 for training, test and development. Table 2 gives average precision, recall and F1 of 2.84, 20.30 and 4.66 on TIB-Core, and 22.99, 27.20, 23.54 (Case 1) and 14.02, 23.39, 16.33 (Case 2) for the qualitative cases. Recall rises with k, with a jump beyond k = 15; English beats German in precision and recall; F1 peaks around k = 15–20; articles and books score higher than conference papers and reports; and lower k favours precision while higher k favours recall.",
