        "text": "End of the quantitative results and the qualitative results. Most records have between 0 and 20 subjects, with an upper quartile of 5 (Figure 3), which the authors use to explain how recall@k varies. Compared with other teams (Figure 2), precision differences are marginal; most teams have high recall@5 but low precision@5, which the authors read as ranking quality mattering more than the LLM module. In the two qualitative case studies, the text gives recall 24.26% and F1 20.06% for Case 1 and recall 19.55% and F1 13.63% for Case 2, figures that differ from the Table 2 averages. By subject class (Figure 4), recall is highest for informatics (about 50%) and technology (45.5% in Case 1, 34.7% in Case 2), and lowest for physics (13.4%, Case 2) and mathematics (20.8%); the text gives both informatics figures as Case 1, apparently meaning one for each case.",
